{% block content %}
<span class="eyebrow">AI Visibility Rankings · Methodology</span>
<h1 class="page-title">How the rankings are produced</h1>
<p class="page-lede">Every industry page at <a href="/ai-visibility">/ai-visibility</a> is generated from a fixed methodology: 8 category-level queries against {{ engine_display_name }} per brand, scored monthly, with a composite ranking that weights being-recommended over being-cited. Here are the specifics so you can audit the data yourself.</p>

<div class="definition-box">
  <div class="label">In one sentence</div>
  <p>For each industry, we run 8 buyer-intent queries against {{ engine_display_name }}, count how often each brand is named in the prose and cited in the source list, compute a <strong>70% visibility + 30% citation</strong> composite score, and re-rank monthly. Same questions every month so the trend is comparable.</p>
</div>

<h2>The 8 queries we ask, per industry</h2>
<p>Identical question shape across every industry — only the category name changes. These are buyer-intent prompts that mirror how AI engines are actually used in research:</p>

<div class="query-list">
<span class="n">1.</span> Best {industry}<br>
<span class="n">2.</span> Top {industry} 2026<br>
<span class="n">3.</span> Best {industry} for small business<br>
<span class="n">4.</span> Top {industry} alternatives<br>
<span class="n">5.</span> How do I choose the right {industry}?<br>
<span class="n">6.</span> {industry} pricing comparison<br>
<span class="n">7.</span> {industry} reviews<br>
<span class="n">8.</span> What is the best {industry} on the market?
</div>

<p style="margin-top:14px;">Eight is the right number: enough to see real patterns (not just single-answer noise from one query), but small enough that the cost stays bounded at ~$0.03/refresh/industry. The shape mirrors the free-preview query set in our paid audits, so the methodology is consistent across products.</p>

<h2>The scoring formula</h2>
<p>For each brand in an industry, we compute two raw metrics:</p>

<div class="formula"><strong>visibility_pct</strong> = (answers_naming_brand / 8) × 100</div>
<div class="formula"><strong>citation_pct</strong> = (answers_citing_brand_domain / 8) × 100</div>

<p>Then the composite that drives the ranking:</p>

<div class="formula"><strong>visibility_score</strong> = visibility_pct × 0.7 + citation_pct × 0.3</div>

<p>The 70/30 weighting reflects an editorial choice — for most brand owners, being named in the AI's prose recommendation matters more than being one of many cited sources. If you weight them differently (e.g. 50/50 because you're optimising for citations as a backlink-equivalent), the ranking shifts but rarely dramatically. The raw <code>visibility_pct</code> and <code>citation_pct</code> are visible on every brand row so you can re-rank with your own weighting.</p>

<h2>Refresh cadence</h2>
<p>Every 30 days by default per industry. The cron worker picks up to 3 industries per 5-minute tick whose <code>next_scheduled_refresh</code> is due, runs the 8 queries, re-scores every brand, snapshots the previous state into history (drives the Movers &amp; Shakers section), generates a fresh AI-written narrative + FAQ from the new data, and advances the schedule.</p>

<ul class="bullets">
  <li>Industries can have custom intervals (some categories shift faster than others) — set per-industry on creation.</li>
  <li>Manual refresh is available via the admin form or <code>POST /api/industries/{slug}/refresh</code> when needed.</li>
  <li>Newly-created industries get an immediate first refresh so the page is populated within ~6 minutes of creation.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What's stored and what's regenerated</h2>
<p>Per refresh, the system updates: visibility + citation percentages per brand, the composite score, rank ordering, per-engine breakdown (currently just Google AI), top cited sources for the whole category, and a fresh AI-generated narrative (3 paragraphs of observations + per-top-5-brand context + 4–6 category-specific FAQs). The previous state is snapshotted into <code>monitor_industry_brand_history</code> so the next refresh can compute Movers &amp; Shakers.</p>

<h2>How the brand list per industry is curated</h2>
<p>We hand-pick ~20 brands per industry from public market-leader sources: G2 Grids for SaaS categories, Crunchbase top-funded lists, trade-press "best X" coverage. The intent is broad coverage of recognised leaders, not exhaustive coverage of every product in the space. If your brand is missing from a category you think you should be in, <a href="/support">send us a support ticket</a> with the industry slug and we'll review.</p>

<h2>What we DON'T do</h2>
<ul class="bullets">
  <li><strong>Take payment for inclusion or position.</strong> Brands cannot pay to be added to a ranking or to rank higher. Period.</li>
  <li><strong>Manipulate the query set per industry.</strong> The 8 queries are identical (modulo industry name) across every category. Brands can't get a friendlier query mix.</li>
  <li><strong>Hide our methodology.</strong> Everything is on this page. The composite formula is reproducible from the raw data shown on every brand row.</li>
  <li><strong>Promise visibility numbers.</strong> AI engines change weekly. We honestly measure where you are; we don't guarantee where you'll be.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How to improve your ranking</h2>
<p>The same way any AEO program works — better content, structured data, entity signals, earned mentions on the sites AI engines trust in your category. The <a href="/answer-engine-optimization-checklist">20-item AEO checklist</a> is the practical playbook. The fastest single move is usually shipping FAQPage schema across your content library.</p>

